# Local spelling-policy caches and helper tool state
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.typos-oxendict-base.json
.typos-oxendict-base.toml
.uv-cache/
.uv-tools/
.vtcode/
memories/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo

# CI-only working directories mounted by the Namespace cache volume
.ci-tools/
.sccache/

# cargo-mutants output. Its default `--out-dir` is `mutants.out` beside the
# workspace, and a run that finds one already there moves it to
# `mutants.out.old` first. Leaving these untracked-and-unignored makes every
# documented local mutation run dirty the working tree.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Coverage profiles. `-Cinstrument-coverage` makes every instrumented test
# binary write a `<name>_<hash>_<pid>.profraw` in the directory it ran in,
# which for a crate's own tests is that crate's source directory — so a
# `cargo llvm-cov` run leaves dozens of them inside `crates/`. The name
# carries a process id, so they accumulate rather than overwrite. They are
# merged by the coverage driver and never need to be committed.
*.profraw
